<DocsLayout title="Getting started" description="Build Hologram Live, initialize its configuration, and start the local service.">
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p>Build the single <code>hologram</code> executable, initialize a typed configuration, and start a local module host in a few commands.</p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Rust 1.88 or newer with Cargo.</li>
    <li><code>just</code> for the repository development recipes.</li>
    <li>Node.js only when building the Astro docs or Tauri desktop frontend.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Build and initialize</h2>
  <pre><code>cargo build --release --locked
./target/release/hologram init</code></pre>
  <p>The generated configuration lives at <code>~/.config/hologram/live.toml</code> on every supported platform. Unknown fields are rejected instead of silently ignored.</p>

  <h2>Start the service</h2>
  <pre><code>./target/release/hologram start
./target/release/hologram status
./target/release/hologram modules list</code></pre>
  <div class="note"><strong>Development loop</strong>Install <code>cargo-watch</code> once, then run <code>just dev</code> to rebuild and restart the foreground server whenever Rust or Protobuf inputs change.</div>

  <h2>Open the interfaces</h2>
  <div class="doc-grid">
    <article class="doc-card"><h3>Status page</h3><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:11435">127.0.0.1:11435</a> confirms the service is reachable.</p></article>
    <article class="doc-card"><h3>API reference</h3><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:11435/docs">/docs</a> renders the self-hosted Scalar reference.</p></article>
  </div>

  <h2>Exercise <code>.holo</code> support</h2>
  <p>Start with <code>hologram app init ./my-app</code> for a guided <code>hologram.json</code>, or use <code>--kind wasm --path app.wasm --entry holo_run</code> for a non-interactive scaffold.</p>
  <pre><code>hologram holo fixture fixture.holo
hologram holo import fixture.holo
hologram holo list</code></pre>
  <p>Import returns a content address that can be inspected and verified with <code>hologram holo inspect</code> and <code>hologram holo verify</code>. See <a href={sitePath('/docs/holo-files')}>the <code>.holo</code> format guide</a> for the binary layout, layer model, identity rules, and application directory.</p>
</DocsLayout>
